---
import GuideLayout from '../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<GuideLayout title="RuneScape Adventure Guide" current="home">
  <section class="hero home-hero">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Two ways to play the same Ironman</div>
      <h1>Pick the amount of guidance you actually want.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The Beginner track is a discovery-first adventure. Intermediate Efficiency is for players who know RuneScape and want a clear order for quests, useful unlocks and training, with relaxed methods and explanations of what to bring and keep.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="hero-card">
      <h2>Same account. Different lens.</h2>
      <p class="quest-meta">Both tracks value meaningful unlocks and long-term account progression. The difference is how much the guide explains, how closely it plans your quests and training, and how much attention it expects from you.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="track-grid" aria-label="Guide tracks">
    <article class="track-card">
      <div class="section-label">Beginner</div>
      <h2>Adventure first</h2>
      <p>For a new player. Quests are introduced as stories and places, hints are layered, and efficient planning stays mostly invisible.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Regional exploration and lore context</li>
        <li>House upgrades as visible milestones</li>
        <li>Minimal spoilers and layered hints</li>
        <li>No expectation that you know the wiki by heart</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="button" href={`${base}chapters/chapter-1/`}>Open Beginner Chapter 1</a>
    </article>

    <article class="track-card intermediate-card">
      <div class="section-label">Intermediate Efficiency</div>
      <h2>BRUHsailer, translated into normal-person RuneScape</h2>
      <p>For players who know the game but do not want to mentally juggle six quests, four diary tasks, three inventories and a compost bin at the same time.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Useful quest, travel and money unlocks in a sensible order</li>
        <li>Quests completed one at a time where possible</li>
        <li>AFK and low-attention skilling preferred when reasonable</li>
        <li>Diary rewards introduced when they help</li>
        <li>What to bring, what to save and when to stop training</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="button" href={`${base}intermediate/`}>Open Intermediate</a>
    </article>
  </section>
</GuideLayout>
